# CQ-12 · direction-contradiction
#
# Question: Does any single document assert two opposite directional values of
#           the same figure/ground pair under the same viewer?
# Persona:  P2 — scene-data annotator / ML researcher. Above and below from one
#           vantage point is the directional counterpart of CQ-11, and the same
#           kind of thing no shape can see.
# Spec:     docs/vson.md §3.3; §5.7 (`vso:directional`); §5.12
# Form:     ASK — a clean corpus answers false
# Note:     The three opposition pairs are listed in both orders, so the answer
#           does not depend on which of the two facts the engine matches first.
#           Same viewer is part of the question: the same pair may legitimately
#           be above from one camera and below from another, which is exactly
#           what clause C5's mandatory viewer exists to keep straight.
PREFIX vso: <https://w3id.org/vson/v1/ontology#>

ASK {
  GRAPH ?doc {
    ?first  a vso:SpatialFact ; vso:figure ?figure ; vso:ground ?ground ;
            vso:viewer ?viewer ; vso:directional ?one .
    ?second a vso:SpatialFact ; vso:figure ?figure ; vso:ground ?ground ;
            vso:viewer ?viewer ; vso:directional ?other .
    VALUES (?one ?other) {
      (vso:above       vso:below)
      (vso:below       vso:above)
      (vso:left_of     vso:right_of)
      (vso:right_of    vso:left_of)
      (vso:in_front_of vso:behind)
      (vso:behind      vso:in_front_of)
    }
  }
}
